Audit complete. Report written to `.build/ui_runs/20260424_153904/ui_audit_current.json`.

**Verdict: GAPS_EXIST** — 5 gaps found, 2 high / 1 medium / 2 low.

---

**High severity (2)**

1. **Violet node radial glow missing** (`OrganismRenderer.swift`)  
   The spec requires a violet radial glow. The renderer only does a sine-wave size pulse — no concentric faded halo rings are drawn behind the node. Fix: add two large-radius, low-alpha makeCircle calls before the violet core circle in `buildVertices()`.

2. **Docker HUD can never show 11/11** (`HealthPoller.swift`)  
   `HealthPoller.poll()` polls only 6 of the 11 services defined in `ServiceHealth.allServices`. Services svc-9002 through svc-9006 are permanently stuck at `.unknown` and never count as online, so the Docker pill tops out at 6/11. Fix: add ports 9002–9006 to the polling list.

**Medium severity (1)**

3. **VoiceOverlayPill shows "dormant" not "ready"** (`AppState.swift`)  
   `voiceState` initializes as `.dormant` → pill reads "Violet · dormant" at launch and whenever services are offline. Spec hard-codes "Violet · ready". Fix: change initial value to `.ready`.

**Low severity (2)**

4. & 5. **Metal layer token violations** (`OrganismRenderer.swift:303–313`, `MetalView.swift:11`)  
   Both files use inline SIMD4/MTLClearColor float literals because Metal can't consume SwiftUI `Color`. Values are numerically correct and commented, but violate the "by name not hardcoded" invariant. Fix: introduce a shared float-constant bridge struct.

Everything else — all 9 design tokens, all 6 left-rail modes routed correctly, organism topology (5 chambers, adj, handrail, kernel inside boundary, build space outside, founder node), right panel sections, bottom timeline color coding, and VoiceOverlay z-order — is on spec.
